WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
This stewardship extends to digital data
practices and protocol management.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.860
All research materials, including metadata
and software, must be rigorously

3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.960
curated and preserved for a clearly stated
duration.

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.620
Data must follow the FAIR principles.

5
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.560
It must be findable, accessible,
interoperable, and reusable.

6
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.220
This involves an access paradigm where
research data is as open as possible,

7
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.820
yet as closed as necessary. When handling
participant data, the General Data

8
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.600
Protection Regulation, or GDPR, provides
the framework for protection and

9
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.340
privacy. Under this framework, raw
datasets and software are recognized as

10
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.820
legitimate, citable products of research.

11
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.320
Under the European Code, data management
is classified as a primary ethical

12
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.360
obligation.
